 5. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Maura Losch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 🔒 Estonia will close its border crossings with Russia on Dec. 1, according to its foreign affairs ministry. "Russia's attempts to intimidate, destabilize or undermine our security," it said on X , "will come with a price."

 Why it matters: The decision follows a failed arson attack on Estonian defense contractor Threod Systems. It was allegedly orchestrated by Russia's GRU intelligence service. 💭 My thought bubble: Estonia's former ambassador to the U.S., Kristjan Prikk, once told me the Russia-Ukraine war is "not only about territory." 🏗️ Hadrian acquired Kutztown Foundry &amp; Machine in Pennsylvania and plans to invest some $300 million to "massively upgrade" the site, to be known as Factory 6, chief executive Chris Power told reporters.

 Why it matters: "We'll be feeding the submarine program, both steel and critical castings made from that steel, from day one," he said. "This is massive, massive, massive heavy industry." 💭 My thought bubble: Hadrian was valued just shy of $8 billion this summer, after a $1.37 billion raise. More on that here . 👀 Northrop Grumman and Hermeus have partnered, with plans to develop and deliver "a new class of autonomous, high‑Mach aircraft." The former's announcement mentions "months, not years."

 Why it matters: The two companies have plenty of airframe, autonomy, electronic warfare, sensing and networking expertise. 💭 My thought bubble: Remember Ramjet-X ? And remember how Hermeus got the green light to manufacture Pratt &amp; Whitney's F100 engine? 🤖 Path Robotics raised $300 million and is now valued just shy of $2.5 billion. The Series E was led by Georgian. Other backers include Drive Capital and IronArc Ventures.

 Why it matters: Path said it's experienced "significant" growth as defense and energy builders, among others, "turn to physical AI to overcome production constraints and expand capacity." 💭 My thought bubble: You can't reindustrialize for tomorrow with yesterday's tools! 
 
